#: ../../source/integrations-guide/incoming-webhooks.rst:7
msgid "**Technical complexity:** :ref:`No-code <no-code>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/incoming-webhooks.rst:9
msgid ""
"Send or receive real-time data from external tools. Webhooks require "
"minimal coding and are easy to set up with virtually any tool or platform"
" because they use lightweight HTTP POST requests with JSON payloads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/incoming-webhooks.rst:11
msgid ""
"Using incoming webhooks in Mattermost requires only basic setup. You "
"generate a webhook URL using the Mattermost interface, then point another"
" service to send data to that address. No coding is required if your "
"external service triggering the events is able to send data via webhooks "
"or HTTP POST requests, which most modern applications and platforms "
"support. Setting this up usually involves pasting the Mattermost webhook "
"URL into the service’s settings and selecting what type of events you "
"want it to send."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/incoming-webhooks.rst:14
msgid "Example Use Cases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/incoming-webhooks.rst:16
msgid "Here are some example use cases for incoming webhooks in Mattermost:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/incoming-webhooks.rst:18
msgid "**Monitoring alerts**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/incoming-webhooks.rst:20
msgid ""
"Send real-time alerts from monitoring systems (such as Prometheus or "
"Datadog) into a dedicated Mattermost channel so your team is immediately "
"notified about system issues or downtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/incoming-webhooks.rst:22
msgid "**Build and deployment notifications**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/incoming-webhooks.rst:24
msgid ""
"Post automated updates from CI/CD pipelines (such as Jenkins or GitLab "
"CI) to a channel, keeping developers informed of build status, test "
"results, and deployment progress."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/incoming-webhooks.rst:26
msgid "**Customer support updates**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/incoming-webhooks.rst:28
msgid ""
"Forward new support ticket notifications from systems like Zendesk or "
"ServiceNow into a support channel, ensuring the team can respond quickly "
"to incoming requests."
msgstr ""

